--- A word asked whether a list holds it (`x in xs`), where the list's
--- items can fail, is still the word after: compiled, the word was moved
--- into the result it was met as and the program did not build (E0382;
--- Lory's drawn page, a widget's key kept after `key in w.list`)
fn named[s]
  if s eq ''
    return error['empty', 'x']
  s
xs = [named['a'], named['b']]
x = 'a'
log[x in xs]
log[x]
log['z' in xs]
log[x not in xs]
fn listed[list, word]
  if word in list
    return 'held `word`'
  'not `word`'
log[listed[xs, x]]
log[listed[xs, 'q']]
